                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jordan+algebra"} Jordan algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonionic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Albert+algebra"} Albert algebra
                that “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizes
                a 4d sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"}> Minkowski spacetime
                ” (see
                %a{:href => "Albert+algebra#StabilizerOf4dMinkowskiInsideOctonionicAlbertAlgebra"} there
                for details).
              %p
                More concretely, it is identified with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%289%29"} Spin(9)
                which respects a splitting
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℍ
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi ℍ
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H} \oplus \mathbb{H} \simeq_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{C} \oplus \mathbb{C}^3
                (
                %a{:href => "Spin%289%29#Krasnov19"}> Krasnov 19
                , see also at
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "GUT#TheGUTKnownAsSO10"} SO(10)-GUT
          %p
            This is part of ongoing speculation that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonion"} octonionic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+structures"} exceptional structures
            might be behind the standard model.
