            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"}> chiral perturbation theory
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "effective+quantum+field+theory#FermiTheoryOfWeakInteractions"} Fermi’s theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alvarez-Gaum%C3%A9"}> Luis Alvarez-Gaumé
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miguel+A.+V%C3%A1zquez-Mozo"} Miguel A. Vázquez-Mozo
              %em Lectures on Field Theory and the Standard Model: A Symmetry-Oriented Approach
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08097"}> arXiv:2306.08097
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p More on the issue of the exact gauge group:
          %ul
            %li#LiXu24
              Hao-Lin Li, Ling-Xiao Xu,
              %em Understanding the SM gauge group from SMEFT
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.04229"}> arXiv:2404.04229
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of Clifford algebras reminiscent of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
            of relevance in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/grand+unified+theories"} grand unified theories
            thereof:
          %ul
            %li#Wilson20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+A.+Wilson"}> Robert A. Wilson
                ,
                %em A group-theorist’s perspective on symmetry groups in physics
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.14613"}> arXiv:2009.14613
                )
            %li#Wilson21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+A.+Wilson"}> Robert A. Wilson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Problem of Choosing Subgroups of Clifford Algebras for Applications in Fundamental Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00006-021-01160-5"} doi:10.1007/s00006-021-01160-5
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "Albert+algebra#ReferencesRelationStandardModel"} Albert algebra – possible relation to color gauge structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"} Matilde Marcolli
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry%2C+Quantum+Fields+and+Motives"} Noncommutative Geometry, Quantum Fields and Motives
          %p Review with outlook “beyond the standard model”:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Langacker"}> Paul Langacker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The standard model and beyond
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.sns.ias.edu/~pgl/talks/neutron.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Langacker05.pdf", :title => ""} Langacker05.pdf
            %li
              %p
                Dmitry Kazakov,
                %em Beyond the Standard Model’ 17
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.00148"}> arXiv:1807.00148
                )
            %li#Wulzer19
              %p
                Andrea Wulzer,
                %em Behind the Standard Model
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.01017"}> arXiv:1901.01017
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Wells"}> James Wells
                ,
                %em The Once and Present Standard Model of Elementary Particle Physics
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04604"}> arxiv:1911.04604
                )
          %h3#ReferencesAnomalyCancellation Anomaly cancellation
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
            on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
          %ul
            %li#HMY13
              %p
                Takaaki Hashimoto, Mamoru Matsunaga, Kenta Yamamoto,
                %em
                  Quantization of hypercharge in gauge groups locally isomorphic but globally nonisomorphic to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi c
                        %mo ×
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi L
                        %mo ×
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(3)_c \times SU(2)_L \times U(1)_Y
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.0669"}> arXiv:1302.0669
                )
            %li
              %p
                Nakarin Lohitsiri,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Tong"} David Tong
                %em Hypercharge Quantisation and Fermat’s Last Theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.00514"}> arXiv:1907.00514
                )
              %p
                (relating to
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermat%27s+last+theorem"} Fermat's last theorem
          %h3#ReferencesHistory History
          %ul
            %li#Bjorken85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Bjorken"}> James Bjorken
              ,
              %em The November Revolution: A Theorist Reminisces
              (1985) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/214067"}> spire:214067
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %blockquote
            %p
              “The big international conference of
              = succeed "1974" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              in London was a turning point
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              Ellis’ catalog well reflected the state of theoretical confusion and general disarray in trying to interpret the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^+ e^-
              data. But in the midst of all of this was a talk by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Iliopoulos"} John Iliopoulos
              (I think I was there too). With passionate zealotry, he laid out with great accuracy what we call the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proton+decay"} proton decay
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charm+quark"} charm
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)\times U(1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electroweak+theory"} electroweak theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(5)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} grand unification
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+field"} Higgs
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Iliopoulos"}> John Iliopoulos
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The rise of the Standard Model
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Physics in the CERN theory division
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/261679?ln=en"} cds:261679
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://cds.cern.ch/record/261679/files/CERN-CH-39.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Kibble"}> Tom Kibble
                ,
                %em The Standard Model of Particle Physics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1412.4094"}> arXiv:1412.4094
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Iliopoulos16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Iliopoulos"}> John Iliopoulos
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The making of the standard theory
                %strong 26
                (2016) 29-59 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1497884"}> spire:1497884
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://cds.cern.ch/record/2217096/files/9789814733519_0002.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steven+Weinberg"}> Steven Weinberg
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Conceptual Basis of the Standard Model: Steven Weinberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://artsci.case.edu/smat50/"} The Standard Model at 50
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/nydSHnv1ABI?list=PLBELrG1nZ2U6H3I1il4NhNVNcdUVUE5Ye"} YT
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Iliopoulos"}> John Iliopoulos
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From Many Models to ONE THEORY
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.10233"} arXiv:2501.10233
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/ECUBXySE0pI"} YT
